Testing that a per-interface ubus data.firewall rule carrying src/dest zone
references is pinned to the publishing interface device (the netifd protocol
handler contract, e.g. 464xlat), while a rule that opts out with an empty
device ("device": "") instead resolves through its zone references. A rule
opting out without any zone reference would end up unscoped in a base chain
and is rejected with a diagnostic.

